  "aggregationRules": [
    "Aggregate within one indicator/dependency group before cross-family confluence.",
    "Do not count level, zone, crossing, slope, persistence and divergence as separate votes by default.",
    "A derived event may be evaluated for timing value, but any incremental claim must control its parent level/path.",
    "Divergence is an interaction between price-pivot geometry and indicator state, not an independent raw evidence family.",
    "Threshold labels are quantizations of continuous fields; they cannot add information beyond the parent value unless path/event timing is explicitly tested."
  ]
